BUSINESS RULE 1 - EARLY LOSS / ECO
============================================================
 
Early Loss / ECO is defined as a contract reaching 120 consecutive
days past due where default started within the first 3 installments
and the contract is within the first 7 months on book.
 
Conceptual rule:
 
IF consecutive_DPD >= 120
AND default_started_within_first_3_installments = TRUE
AND MOB <= 7
THEN Flag_ECO = 1
 
ECO charge-off occurs between MOB 4 and MOB 7.
 
Maintain ECO_Type as an explainable classification:
 
FPD = First Payment Default
EPD = Early Payment Default
 
Do not replace FPD/EPD with a generic risk label.
 
============================================================
BUSINESS RULE 2 - POTENTIAL ECO
============================================================
 
Potential ECO is the CORE EARLY-WARNING indicator.
 
A contract is Potential ECO only when:
 
- DPD > 30
- default started within the first 3 installments
- contract is still inside the Early Loss observation window
- contract is not already ECO
 
ECO and Potential ECO must be mutually exclusive.
 
IF Flag_ECO = 1
THEN Flag_Potential = 0
 
Potential_Period must be calculated RELATIVE to the
snapshot/cut-off month.
 
91-120 DPD -> M+1
61-90 DPD  -> M+2
31-60 DPD  -> M+3
 
Never hard-code specific YYYYMM values.
 
If delinquency started after the first 3 installments or falls outside
the applicable Early Loss window, do NOT classify it as Potential ECO.
 
Classify it as Late Delinquency.
 
